ent-side navigation, no next/image, and no error to say so. An app that composes NextAdapterProvider (or AdapterProvider with nextAdapters) itself is already covered.","layout.shorthands":"Use fill not fillWidth fillHeight; center not horizontal=\"center\" vertical=\"center\"; Row/Column not Flex direction=, and Row for a Flex with no direction (Flex defaults to row). Flex is for a direction that changes at a breakpoint.","layout.defaults":"Never write props equal to defaults or implied by another prop on the element: position=\"relative\", direction on Row/Column, variant=\"primary\" on Button, fillWidth beside maxWidth (maxWidth already fills the width), minWidth={0} beside fillWidth (fillWidth already sets min-width: 0).","layout.responsiveProps":"Responsive xl/l/m/s/xs props exist only on Flex, Row, Column and Grid. Button, Text, Heading and the rest have none: to change one at a breakpoint, wrap it in a Row or Column and put the breakpoint prop there (s={{ hide: true }}).","size.rem":"A number on width, height, minWidth or minHeight is rem, not px: width={32} is 512 px. For a pixel size write the spacing token string, width=\"32\" (32 px), or the rem value, width={2}. An icon or avatar box is usually \"24\" to \"48\".","spacing.tokens":"gap, padding and margin take spacing tokens (\"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", \"12\", \"16\", \"20\", \"24\", \"32\", \"40\", \"48\", \"56\", \"64\", \"72\", \"80\", \"104\", \"128\", \"160\", or xs–xl). \"6\" and \"10\" are not tokens and are type errors.","layout.noSpanOrType":"Row, Column and Grid have no span and no type prop. A clickable row is a Button (or a native <button>), and a Grid child spanning columns uses style={{ gridColumn: \"span 2\" }}."},"quality":{"mdx":"mdxComponents, or createMdxComponents({...}) to replace an element or register a tag, from @once-ui-system/core/mdx — never a hand-written element map","trail":"Breadcrumbs above the title; the last item has no href and is the current page","width":"Articl